TEXT -96 -200 Left 3 ;#54 Current in an inductor: current lags voltage
TEXT -96 -144 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykgmKOVkyW0
TEXT -96 -104 Left 2 ;L1 has about 1 kohm of reactance at 741 kHz (Alan's test frequency); R2 senses the series current.
TEXT -96 -72 Left 2 ;The current (CH2) peaks after the applied voltage (CH1): in an inductor the current lags the voltage.
TEXT 480 16 Left 2 ;CH1: generator voltage applied to the top of L1 (Alan's channel 1).
TEXT 480 48 Left 2 ;CH2: drop across the 100 ohm sense resistor R2, so CH2 = 100 ohms x current.
TEXT 480 80 Left 2 ;V1: 741 kHz, 1.7 V p-p as on Alan's scope; Rser = 50 ohms is the generator's output resistance.
TEXT 480 160 Left 2 !.param f=741k
TEXT 480 200 Left 2 !.tran 0 20u 0 1n
TEXT 480 240 Left 2 !.meas tran TV WHEN V(ch1)=0 RISE=1 TD=15.6u
TEXT 480 272 Left 2 !.meas tran TI WHEN V(ch2)=0 RISE=1 TD=15.6u
TEXT 480 304 Left 2 !.meas tran LEAD_DEG PARAM (TV-TI)*f*360
TEXT 480 336 Left 2 !.meas tran CH1_PP PP V(ch1) FROM 10u TO 20u
TEXT 480 368 Left 2 !.meas tran CH2_PP PP V(ch2) FROM 10u TO 20u
